<Page
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What information Patriotic Angler collects, and what it doesn't."
  lede="Short version: this site doesn't use tracking cookies or ad trackers, and we don't sell anything about you."
>
  <p><em>Last updated November 6, 2026.</em></p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Netlify, keeps standard request logs (such as IP address, browser type and the
      page requested) to run and protect the site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages you send.</strong> If you use the contact form, we receive your name, email address and message.
      We use them only to reply to you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't set advertising or analytics cookies.</li>
    <li>We don't sell or share your information with marketers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Links to Amazon and other sites</h2>
  <p>
    When you click a link to Amazon or another site, you're on their site and under their privacy policy. Amazon uses
    cookies to know a purchase came from our link so it can credit us. Amazon's privacy notice is linked at the bottom
    of every page on Amazon.com.
  </p>

  <h2>Photos</h2>
  <p>Some photos load from Unsplash, which receives a standard request from your browser when the image loads.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If we add anything that collects more information, we'll update this page first. Questions?
    <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
